  "scientific_scope": {
    "original_status": "pipeline demonstration",
    "transition_grid": "14x14x1 (196 k), used as both the coarse and the fine grid",
    "caveats": [
      "The 14x14x1 mesh does not contain K, so the mesh QP gap and the exciton binding energy are not converged with respect to the k mesh.",
      "The G0W0 step used the pyatb velocity source that reads the velocity_matrix ABACUS wrote, not the native H(R)/S(R)/r(R) differentiation.",
      "LibBSE ran with bse_use_fine_kgrid 0: the coarse and fine grids are the same 196-point mesh, so no interpolation to a denser grid was applied.",
      "Two GW entries on the 121-point path (bands 62 and 67) are nonfinite where the QPE solver failed. Both lie far outside the plotted near-gap window (bands 10-17) and are kept visible in the archived table rather than removed.",
      "The exciton density slices were reconstructed from the BSE amplitudes with alter_excitons_gw_bse_20261105/scripts/exciton_density_from_amplitudes.py, patched in three documented ways: the l<=3 harmonics were added (this basis has an f shell), per-atom orbital blocks were sized from each species (Mo 44, S 22), and the band window offset was set to LibBSE's reported core offset 9 so the amplitudes pair with bands 10-17 instead of 1-8. Without the third patch the electron density peaks at S rather than at Mo.",
      "eps2 is normalised by the primitive-cell volume 1777.44 bohr^3, taken from |a1 x a2| * c with a1 = 3.184 A and c = 30 A. The hexagonal form (sqrt(3)/2) a^2 c gives the same number; multiplying it by 3 is a common slip and would understate eps2 by a factor of three.",
      "The eps2 normalisation was checked against the f-sum rule: integrating omega*eps2 to 30 eV gives 0.0948 in Hartree units, against the analytic 2*pi^2*sum(f_phys)/(N_k*V) = 0.0947, a ratio of 1.001. The 33% figure spectrum_to_eps2.py prints is the band-window completeness (4 occupied + 4 empty of 88 bands), not a normalisation deficit."
    ]
  }
